# Responsive Design

Whenever you implement or change any UI/design, you MUST verify responsiveness
BEFORE reporting the task as done.

## Rules
- Use **container query variants** (`@sm:` `@md:` `@lg:` `@xl:`), NOT viewport breakpoints (`sm:` `md:` `lg:`).
- See `.cursor/rules/mobile-first-design.mdc` for the full token and container query reference.
- Grids/flex must reflow based on container width. Prefer `grid-cols-1 @md:grid-cols-2 @lg:grid-cols-3`.
- Avoid fixed pixel widths that break mobile. Use `w-full`, `max-w-*`, and `min-w-0`.
- Long text must wrap or truncate (`truncate`, `break-words`).
- Touch targets: use `min-h-touch` (44px touch / 32px desktop), never `w-6 h-6`.
- Typography: use `text-body`, `text-sub`, `text-label` — never `text-[11px]`.
- Icons: use `w-icon-sm h-icon-sm`, never `w-3 h-3`.

## Container Query Breakpoints (Tailwind v4)

| Variant | Min container width |
|---------|---------------------|
| `@sm` | 384px (24rem) |
| `@md` | 448px (28rem) |
| `@lg` | 512px (32rem) |
| `@xl` | 576px (36rem) |

These are NOT the same as viewport breakpoints (640/768/1024/1280).

## Example
```tsx
// BAD: viewport breakpoints, hardcoded sizes
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
<button className="text-[11px] px-2 py-1.5 w-6 h-6">
  <X className="w-3 h-3" />
</button>

// GOOD: container queries, token-based
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 @md:grid-cols-2 @lg:grid-cols-3">
<button className="min-h-touch px-4 text-button font-medium flex items-center gap-2">
  <X className="w-icon-sm h-icon-sm" />
  Close
</button>
```
